 "final_text": "Answer submitted. Here's the reply for Sam:\n\n---\n\n**Reply to Sam Rivera:**\n\nFound it \u2014 but it's outside the system. You emailed Meadow Analytics the invoice directly on 2/6, because their vendor setup in D365 was still pending (that's the \"log it in a manual tracker\" note in your fwd to AR). It never got posted to Books or the ERP \u2014 I confirmed both show zero records for Meadow Analytics at all: no customer, no invoice, no transaction.\n\n- **Invoice:** INV-2026-047, dated 2/6/2026, $18,750, due 3/8/2026\n- **Client response:** they confirmed receipt on 2/24 and said it was queued for their March payment run, ahead of the due date\n- **But:** no payment was ever recorded on our side \u2014 no Payment object, no AR entry, nothing in either system to confirm the $18,750 actually landed\n\nSo as far as our books are concerned, it's a **$18,750 unreconciled receivable** \u2014 either it got paid and just never got booked (worth checking the bank feed for a March deposit from Meadow), or it's sitting unbilled/uncollected because the manual tracker never made it into the real system. Either way, Meadow needs a proper customer record created and this invoice posted for real.",
